    "body": "### Problem\n\nIf the program output equals or more lines than the window size. Last line of the output will be overwritten by \"[Program exited 0]\" message.\n\nThis is the minimum code to reproduce the issue.\n\n```c\n#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main(int argc, char *argv[]) {\n    int maxlines = 100;\n    for (int i=0; i<maxlines; i++) {\n        printf(\"meow\\n\");\n    }\n    printf(\"LAST LINE\");\n}\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Compiles the code above\n2. Execute with :term ./the-binary or :RunCode with [code_runner.nvim](https://github.com/crag666/code_runner.nvim)\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nPrints out `LAST LINE` at last line\n```\nmeow\nmeow\nmeow\nmeow\nmeow\nLAST LINE\n[Program exited 0]\n```\n\n**Actual behavior:**\nAssume the `window size <= 6`. Last line will be hidden by `[Program exited 0]` message\n```\nmeow\nmeow\nmeow\nmeow\nmeow\n[Program exited 0]  <-- \"LAST LINE\" is here\n```\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.12.4\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno, vim 9.1\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nmacOS 27.0.1\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nWarp v0.2026.09.30.08.29.stable_01\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nhomebrew",
